--
Header-free mimic of libstdc++'s std::function dispatch, cvise-reduced
from cpp17_std_function_lambda_call: the callable is stored through the
_Function_handler pattern and invoked via the _M_invoker function
pointer; symex never reaches the closure body, so the by-reference
update is lost and the assertion wrongly fails ([func.wrap.func.inv]).
g++/clang++ accept and run clean (exit 0).
Update 2026-07-28: the reference-type functional-cast layer is fixed
([expr.type.conv]/1); the residual is the expansion of
`_ArgTypes(__args)...` over the replicated FUNCTION parameter pack in
the member instance (the argument list arrives empty at the cast) --
the concretized-pack family.
Remaining-layer minimal reproducer: cpp17_pack_cast_fn_type_spec.
